    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a sandpiper character. Draw this exact sandpiper character as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the round speckled body with its pale cream chest and short tail feathers, facing right as in image 1, without head, without legs and WITHOUT ANY WING: where the wing lies on the body in image 1, draw only plain speckled body feathers, no wing shape, no long wing feathers and no wing outline on it; its top, normally under the head, rounded.\n2. the head: the round speckled head, facing right as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eye, no beak — keep the rosy cheek; its bottom edge rounded.\n3. the folded wing: the brown speckled wing folded as it lies on the body in image 1, drawn whole, with a rounded shoulder.\n4. the open wing: the same wing spread out wide as in flight, its brown speckled flight feathers fanned, with a rounded shoulder.\n5. one leg: a thin dark leg with its three long toes, drawn whole and straight from the top of the leg, with a rounded top.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a sandpiper character; image 2 shows the same sandpiper cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the sandpiper's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the sandpiper in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the sandpiper's eye as it is in image 1: a dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: the pupil looking down, its upper lid drooping and tilted, a thin shine of a welling tear along the bottom rim.\n6. the same eye crying: gently squeezed shut, a soft downward-curving line (a sad closed eye, not a smile), a few small lashes, and one small light-blue teardrop just below it.\n7. the beak as it is in image 1: the long thin dark beak, closed.\n8. the same beak a little open, peeping.\n9. the same beak wide open, peeping loudly.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    },
