      "size": "1024x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a sandpiper character; image 2 shows the same sandpiper cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw one single piece, centred on the sheet: the sandpiper's head together with its neck, as one piece. It is exactly the head of image 2 — the same round speckled head, the same rosy cheek, the same completely blank face (no eye, no beak), facing right the same way, the same drawing style, colours, texture and line — but there is no chin line under it: the pale cream throat and the speckled back of the neck carry straight on down below the head, as wide as the head, for about half the head's height, the way the head flows into the body in image 1, and end in a smooth rounded bottom edge. At the size the head has in image 1. Nothing else on the sheet. No text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    }
